{
  "version": 3,
  "title": "What if you could turn invisible?",
  "series": "Field Study / Platform Three",
  "pacing": "micro",
  "narration": "Go invisible on a subway platform and the first thing you lose isn't your reflection. It's the train. Everyone else can see those bright windows right through your face, but try looking back at them. Normally your lens bends light from a window onto the back of your eye, where your retina catches it and sends your brain the picture. If light sails straight through your retina too, that train could fill your whole view and you wouldn't see a thing. Want your eyesight back? Some light has to stop inside your eyes. So now there's a pair of eyeballs on platform three, watching everybody else miss their train.",
  "voiceover": "episodes/invisible-voice.wav",
  "music": {
    "track": "episodes/invisible-score.wav",
    "volume": 0.37
  },
